    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d428">

                <pb facs="0501" n="489" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg489"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Bulgaria)/11–1744:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Mr. Alexander C. Kirk,
                        Political Adviser, Allied Force Headquarters at Caserta</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-23T18:00:00-04:00">November 23,
                            1944—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>419. Your 1356, November 17, 9 p.m.<anchor n="58" xml:id="d428-f1"/> Department
                    is informed by Joint Chiefs that Major General John A. Crane was designated on
                    November 17 as Chief of United States Military Representation on the Allied
                    Control Commission for Bulgaria. He has been ordered to proceed to Sofia from
                    Caserta as soon as possible. Two additional <pb facs="0502" n="490"
                        xml:id="pg490"/> Army members and a Navy member will shortly be designated
                    and ordered to Sofia. Please inform Barnes.</p>
                <p>Sent to Caserta, repeated to London and Moscow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
